### Throttle cable

  Grease the throttle-cable inner wires at the pulley wheel of the APS.

<PIC:Manual09_263>
{{image description: Two-panel engine service diagram showing a tool or lever applied to a cable or linkage near the engine. Black arrows point to the service points in each panel.}}

Steering cable ball joints and inner wire Grease the steering cable and shift cable ball joints at the jet thrust nozzles. Extend the steering cable and shift cable inner wires and apply a thin coat of grease to them.

<PIC:Manual09_264>
{{image description: Jet pump or steering linkage diagram with several black arrows pointing to grease points, fittings, and linkage joints around the drive housing.}}

### Pivot points

Grease all pivot points of the steering and shift mechanism at the pump end.

<PIC:Manual09_265>
{{image description: Similar jet pump or drive housing diagram with arrows pointing to fittings, linkage joints, and a lower support or pivot area.}}

- Bearing housings
Grease the bearing housing through the grease nipples.  NOTICE:  Fill the grease slowly and carefully, because it can damage the hoses and the joints.  The first service should be done after 10 hours or 1 month by a Boat Dealer. Fill the bearing housings with water-resistant grease through the grease nipples.

